msgid "dia.sancho.bark.001"
msgstr "By all the saints, it's a mill."

msgid "dia.sancho.bark.002"
msgstr "Master, they're only stones and wood."

msgid "dia.quixote.bark.001"
msgstr "Woe upon you, mortal beast! I will cleave you from your shoulders!"

msgid "dia.quixote.bark.002"
msgstr "I know your kind. I know the mischief you have done in the world."

# --- B5: THE REACTIONS -----------------------------------------------------
# The line a character says when the world moves under them. The key is
# composed: dia.<character>.reaction.<thing>.<book|reality>. "book" is the
# reading they have just arrived at, not the one they left.

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "A giant! Look at it, a giant! There is no wind in my books!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the windmill as a windmill again.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.windmill.reality"
msgstr "Ah. A windmill. Only a windmill. Forgive me, Sancho."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a book.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.book"
msgstr "A book! Look, a book! Who put it here?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quixote sees the rock as a rock again.
msgid "dia.quixote.reaction.rock.reality"
msgstr "A stone. A stone where a book was a moment ago. Forgive me."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a giant.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.windmill.book"
msgstr "Er... that mill has gone giant."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the windmill as a windmill again.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.windmill.reality"
msgstr "There it is. A mill, as always."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the rock as a book.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.rock.book"
msgstr "The stone has turned into a book, master."

#. TRANSLATORS: Sancho sees the rock as a rock again.
msgid "dia.sancho.reaction.rock.reality"
msgstr "A stone. Only a stone."

msgid "tip.lectura.intro"
msgstr "Hold on to the page. Some things only show themselves to a patient eye."

msgid "tip.switch.intro"
msgstr "Change companion. The world is the same; only the reading differs."

msgid "tip.posada.intro"
msgstr "Rest, and the road will still be there."

# --- BOOK LAYER -------------------------------------------------------
# The 1605 original is CONTENT and stays in Spanish in every build. It lives in
# assets/manifiesto/*.json. Only the ".modern" strings are translated.

msgid "bk.ch08.molinos.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"And there appeared to him some thirty or forty monstrous mills that stand "
"on the plain, and so great and tall that they cover the millraces, and "
"the sails of them, going round, made such a din that it seemed as if the "
"winds were grinding the wheat there."

msgid "bk.ch23.montesinos.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"And he told him how he had found a certain enchanted cave in that place, "
"and how a knight came out of it, and how he was leaving him now to go and "
"seek him."

msgid "bk.ch26.galimatias.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"It must be one of three things: the widow is in love with the youth, and "
"the youth with the maiden, and the maiden with neither."

msgid "bk.ch50.impertinente.01.modern"
msgstr ""
"For the tale of the Curious Impertinent is the one I would have written, "
"were it not that my pen is not so bold as to paint the charm of the love "
"that was in it."

