# --- THE FACES: what a character perceives -------------------------------
# One face per truth, per object. The Examine panel shows ONE of them —
# the one the reader is reading right now — and never the other truth and
# never the other character's reading.
#
# The "tell" is the seam: the one detail that does not add up. It is the
# seed of the Lectura system (GDD.md §6), and it is the only thing the
# player is meant to notice without a marker.

#. TRANSLATORS: The rock in the Reality truth: how it looks.
msgid "ui.face.rock.reality.desc"
msgstr "A grey stone about the size of a fist, with dry lichen on the top and its base sunk into the earth."

#. TRANSLATORS: The rock in the Reality truth: the one detail that does not add up.
msgid "ui.face.rock.reality.tell"
msgstr "It is heavier than a stone that size should be."

#. TRANSLATORS: The rock in the Book truth: how it looks.
msgid "ui.face.rock.book.desc"
msgstr "A small book, bound in brown leather and tied with a strap. The edges of the leaves are gilt and they stain your fingers."

#. TRANSLATORS: The rock in the Book truth: the one detail that does not add up.
msgid "ui.face.rock.book.tell"
msgstr "It is heavier than a book that size should be."

#. TRANSLATORS: The title written on the cover of the book the rock is.
msgid "ui.face.rock.book.title"
msgstr "The Ingenious Gentleman Don Quixote of La Mancha"

#. TRANSLATORS: The windmill in the Reality truth: how it looks.
msgid "ui.face.windmill.reality.desc"
msgstr "A stone mill with its four sails spread and a low door, so worn that the hinge no longer fits."

#. TRANSLATORS: The windmill in the Reality truth: the one detail that does not add up.
msgid "ui.face.windmill.reality.tell"
msgstr "There is no wind at all, and yet the sails are turning."

#. TRANSLATORS: The windmill in the Book truth: how it looks.
msgid "ui.face.windmill.book.desc"
msgstr "A giant of the kind that stories are made of, with arms so long they brush the ground and a small head sunk between his shoulders."

#. TRANSLATORS: The windmill in the Book truth: the one detail that does not add up.
msgid "ui.face.windmill.book.tell"
msgstr "What looks like an arm on him is a mill's sail."

